request.description:
The roster read. Two things here are contract rather than data, and both would break `admin-users.js` *silently* if they were wrong:

* the wrapper is **`{ users: [...] }`** — the page's first render reads `resp.users` and its `.catch()` falls back to localStorage seeds, so a bare array would show demo rows as if they were real ones;
* the id key is **`id`**, not the `userId` the session shape uses. The page builds `data-edit` / `data-toggle` / `data-delete` from `u.id`, so the wrong name would leave every row action pointing at a fabricated id (risk R16, on a new surface).
